Exact-head evidence for `71bebdd1a4090c88b2f5eb525a880d522529c0a5`, addressing the fresh review's final-effect, existing-state, and test-cost questions.

The bounded probe ran the production recovery entry, command recovery binding, admitted source assertion, pending-final marker, and durable automatic sender. A controlled in-process Gateway receiver supplied synthetic model output. The final channel adapter performed a real task-local file append only after the production platform-dispatch/handoff guards. This is isolated component-boundary proof, not an external channel or model run.

Each case first persisted and closed its SQLite state, then reopened it for recovery. For revocation cases, the probe waited for actual recovery adoption and held the production adapter-preparation boundary before cancelling the task or changing its requester. It did not manually clear the aborted marker or bypass a source guard.

| Case | Recovery dispatches | Physical final writes | Pending queue entries | Observed outcome |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
| Allowed completion | 1 | 1 | 0 | Task delivery became delivered |
| Cancelled after dispatch | 1 | 0 | 0 | Non-retryable handoff rejection; task remained cancelled |
| Requester reassigned after dispatch | 1 | 0 | 0 | Non-retryable handoff rejection; completion remained pending for its owner |
| Saved delegated session with an unowned pending final | 0 | 0 | 0 | Tombstone and actionable `/new` or `/reset` notice; repeated recovery stayed inert |

Both revoked cases reported `OPENCLAW_PLATFORM_MESSAGE_NOT_DISPATCHED`, caused by `SESSION_WORK_START_CHANGED`, with `retryable=false`, `sentBeforeError=false`, and released queue custody. The allowed case traversed the same sender and produced exactly one file write. All processes and fixture workers joined, and their temporary state was removed.

**Maintainer disposition:** ending automatic replay after the process-bound delegated sender authority is lost is intentional, including an unowned pending final. The transcript and replacement-session guidance remain available. A durable queue owner still retains its independent delivery responsibility; direct inputs and valid completion claims remain retryable after read faults. This accepts the documented continuity tradeoff without reconstructing authority from provenance or an old run ID. Persisted formats and updater/migration code are unchanged; the existing-state result above is a cold-reopened SQLite recovery check, not a published-installer test.

**Measured cost:** the complete final owning file passed **222/222 with one worker**, in **423.27 seconds command wall time** (405.71 seconds within Vitest) on the shared macOS host with Node 24.21.0. The seven added cases' reported durations sum to 16.591 seconds within that serial run; this is not a counterfactual baseline delta. Ordinary [CI run 36085089085](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/36085089085) passed at this exact head on attempt 1; its start-to-completion span was **32m 36s including queue time**. No deadlines or assertions were relaxed.

The initial standalone probe setup failures are retained separately and are not counted as passing evidence: a Vitest-only registry reset was replaced with the production reload owner, and the receiver was corrected to honor execution-start/adoption ordering before final-marker persistence. The four successful cases below use the unchanged published source.

